{"title":"2000 SMT/Algebra Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/a/d3acb3f291a9bfd65911c4ea8dd30d283559cc04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x| + 5 &lt; 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02ddff4ebdbdd28098a0731b1f42317306120e75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x - 3| &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2000 SMT/Algebra Problems/Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Evaluate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/4/6844e3e4929203279b8feb58aba5dce160ed5471.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2000^{3} - 1999 \\cdot 2000^{2} - 1999^{2} \\cdot 2000 + 1999^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"339\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2000 SMT/Algebra Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Five students take a test on which any integer score from 0 to 100 inclusive is possible. What is the largest possible difference between the median and the mean of the scores?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2000 SMT/Algebra Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the fewest number of multiplications required to reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/6/b1653833651a71a5912a387441582cbc76283a80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2000}$\" width=\"36\" height=\"15\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, using only previously\ngenerated powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />? For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/e/a4e7cd088b67abd69d1f9d9f586f38e1b9df46ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\to x^{2} \\to x^{4} \\to x^{8} \\to x^{16} \\to x^{32} \\to x^{64} \\to x^{128} \\to x^{256} \\to x^{512} \\to x^{1024} \\to x^{1536} \\to x^{1792} \\to x^{1920} \\to x^{1984} \\to x^{2000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"883\" height=\"17\" /> uses 15 multiplications\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2000 SMT/Algebra Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A jacket was originally priced at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/3/fb3b9e046c83ca25ffa3c15f213a16571b36a47b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />100. The price was reduced by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b56bd637cb2c936d539be1b5000a64a898af389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> three times and increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b56bd637cb2c936d539be1b5000a64a898af389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> four times in some order. To the nearest cent, what was the final price?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2000 SMT/Algebra Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Barbara, Edward, Abhinav, and Alex took turns writing this test. Working alone, they could finish it in 10, 9, 11, and 12 days, respectively. If only one person works on the test per day, and nobody works on it unless everyone else has spent at least as many days working on it, how many days (an integer) did it take to write this test?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2000 SMT/Algebra Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is called multiplicatively perfect if the product of all the positive divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />. Determine the number of positive multiplicatively perfect numbers less than 100.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2000 SMT/Algebra Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A man has three daughters. The product of their ages is 168, and he remembers that the sum of their ages is the number of trees in his yard. He counts the trees but cannot determine any of their ages. What are all possible ages of his oldest daughter?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2000 SMT/Algebra Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/7/da74258e200762e7d73f279a6412d859e03290ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{c}=\\frac{b}{d} = \\frac{3}{4}, \\sqrt{a^2+b^2}-\\sqrt{b^2+d^2} = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"300\" height=\"38\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/1/8919d26a44c109622c61fdb9057fa6b023b71401.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ac+bd-ad-bc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"136\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2000 SMT/Algebra Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the smallest positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/c/82c2a6f8eb48f99e49ad1f595a55ab958a54cb6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4 + a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> is not prime for any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2000 SMT/Algebra Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Stanford_Mathematics_Tournament\" title=\"Stanford Mathematics Tournament\">Stanford Mathematics Tournament</a></li></ul>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Stanford_Mathematics_Tournament_Problems\" title=\"Stanford Mathematics Tournament Problems\">SMT Problems and Solutions</a></li></ul>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT\" title=\"2000 SMT\">2000 SMT</a></li></ul>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_SMT/Algebra\" title=\"2000 SMT/Algebra\">2000 SMT/Algebra</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018044757\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.035 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 137/1000000\nPost‐exp